Reporting the second occurrence rather than the first is deliberate: the first
one is the entry the user probably meant to keep, so highlighting the later
duplicate is what a form should do.

## Hint 3

Dates: `Number.isNaN(Date.parse(value))` is the check, and `Date.parse` is
reliable for full ISO 8601 strings (it is not, historically, for anything
else — which is why the schema should have constrained the format first).
Compare with `Date.parse(a) < Date.parse(b)` on the numbers rather than
constructing two `Date` objects to compare with `<`, which works but relies on
implicit `valueOf` coercion that a reader has to stop and verify.

