## Problem 5 — a JWT verifier that cannot be talked into anything

Edit `ex5/solution.ts`. Export `signJwt` and `verifyJwt`, HS256 only, built on
`node:crypto`.

```ts
function signJwt(claims: Record<string, unknown>,
  opts: { secret: string; kid?: string; now: number; ttlSeconds: number }): string;

function verifyJwt(token: string,
  opts: { secret: string; now: number; skewSeconds?: number;
          issuer?: string; audience?: string }):
  | { ok: true; claims: Record<string, unknown> }
  | { ok: false; code: string };
```

`signJwt` emits `base64url(header).base64url(payload).base64url(mac)` with
header `{ alg: "HS256", typ: "JWT" }` plus `kid` when given, and adds
`iat = floor(now / 1000)` and `exp = iat + ttlSeconds`.

`verifyJwt` codes, in the order they are checked:

- `malformed` — not three non-empty parts, or either JSON block will not parse;
- `unexpected_alg` — the header's `alg` is anything but `"HS256"`, including
  `"none"`;
- `bad_signature` — constant-time comparison failed;
- `missing_exp` — no numeric `exp`;
- `expired` — `exp` is before `now/1000` minus the skew;
- `not_yet_valid` — `nbf` is after `now/1000` plus the skew;
- `wrong_issuer` / `wrong_audience` — when the option is supplied and the claim
  does not match (`aud` may be a string or an array of strings).

`skewSeconds` defaults to 60. Times are **seconds**.

```
uv run dojo test node v3nb04_auth_sessions_tokens ex5
```

